╭ Set up NetworkManager ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ ● NetworkManager is not running                                                                  │
│ Nexus manages networks through NetworkManager and it is not answering on the system bus,         │
│ although it is installed.                                                                        │
│                                                                                                  │
│ ● systemd-networkd is also managing your network                                                 │
│                                                                                                  │
│ Switch off what manages your network now, then start NetworkManager. The steps are in order.     │
│   $ sudo sys╭ Run the fix? ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮             │
│   $ sudo sys│ NetworkManager is not running                                        │             │
│             │                                                                      │             │
│ Press f to r│ These commands will run:                                             │             │
│             │   $ sudo systemctl disable --now systemd-networkd.service            │             │
│             │   $ sudo systemctl enable --now NetworkManager.service               │             │
│             │                                                                      │             │
│             │ They run as administrator: your system will ask for your password.   │             │
